# Fungus Master — a Two-color Lesser enemy of the 1997 game, the deck as the original shipped it.
# tier: 4/12 Two-color Lesser enemies — 16 life, bribe 70 gold
# enemy: Fungus Master (1997 in-game name, s30/assets/text/Advstrings.txt @CREATURENAMES)
# designer: Coyote Tex, MicroProse designer/producer — every enemy deck (precon page, ref. 2)
# variant: Original (base game; the enemy deck files are dated 19 September 1996)
# source: ../shandalar-src/Decks.zip:Decks/0094.dck "Fungus Master (G/U, 4th)" [Tier 3 —
#   Manalink 3 file dated 2016-02-15; its first 14 maindeck lines are the 1997 deck, the 15
#   lines (60 cards) after them are the modern deck Manalink appended and are NOT shipped; its
#   .vNone/.v<Colour> sections are the 1997 colour-keyed swaps]
# source: ../s30/assets/configs/rogues/fungus_master.toml (main_cards, sideboard_cards, level 4)
#   [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix above]
# source: ../mage-go/rogue_dck/fungus_master.dck [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix]
# cross-check: https://mtg.wiki/page/Shandalar_Enemy_Decks_(Lesser) — "Fungus Master" (Original)
#   [Tier-web — maindeck agrees]
# group: 1997 originals
name: Fungus Master
11 Forest
11 Island
4 Prodigal Sorcerer
4 Fungusaur
3 Ironroot Treefolk
2 Wall of Brambles
4 Rod of Ruin
2 Carnivorous Plant
2 Untamed Wilds
2 Wild Growth
2 Wall of Wood
2 Oasis
4 Regeneration
4 Unsummon
3 Power Sink
# The 1997 file's colour-keyed sideboard sections. The AI played the maindeck WITHOUT
# .vNone plus the one section matching the player's deck colour (.vNone by default);
# .vNone is folded into the maindeck above, and SB: holds, per name, the largest
# colour-section count minus the .vNone count — the smallest sideboard from which
# every 1997 configuration can be rebuilt by swapping.
#   .vNone   3 Power Sink
#   .vBlack  1 Power Sink, 2 Kormus Bell
#   .vBlue   3 Power Sink
#   .vGreen  2 Living Lands, 1 Power Sink
#   .vRed    3 Power Sink
#   .vWhite  3 Power Sink
SB: 2 Kormus Bell
SB: 2 Living Lands
